        <h3 class="sa-regime__name">Positive</h3>
        <div class="sa-regime__value">Moran's I ≈ +0.7</div>
        <p class="sa-regime__note">Hot spots, cold spots, clusters. The default in the real world: income, disease prevalence, language, retail density.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="tool-plate"><canvas id="p2" width="180" height="180"></canvas></div>
        <h3 class="sa-regime__name">Random</h3>
        <div class="sa-regime__value">Moran's I ≈ 0</div>
        <p class="sa-regime__note">The null hypothesis. Rare in the wild but the baseline you test against before claiming a pattern is real.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="tool-plate"><canvas id="p3" width="180" height="180"></canvas></div>
        <h3 class="sa-regime__name">Negative</h3>
        <div class="sa-regime__value">Moran's I ≈ −0.9</div>
        <p class="sa-regime__note">A literal weave. Almost always engineered: competition, territorial rules, or sampling design.</p>
